--TEST--
`Core\Server::traceId` returns a new 32-character id when the request's `traceparent` is malformed, and never the header's text — `rule:observability/a-trace-id-exists-for-every-request`
--HEADERS--
traceparent: 00-4BF92F3577B34DA6A3CE929D0E0E4736-00f067aa0ba902b7-01
--FILE--
<?nvs
// Upper-case hex is not a valid `traceparent`, so the request continues no
// trace. It still has an id: the server draws a new one. Its value is random,
// so the case checks its length and that it is not the header's id.
string $id = Core\Server::traceId();
echo Core\Str::length($id), "\n";
if (Core\Str::lower($id) == '4bf92f3577b34da6a3ce929d0e0e4736') {
    echo "the header's id\n";
} else {
    echo "a new id\n";
}
if (Core\Str::lower($id) == $id) {
    echo "lower case\n";
} else {
    echo "upper case\n";
}
--EXPECT--
32
a new id
lower case
